`huginn validate` now warns with the code `redundant_test_case` when two or more test cases are copies of each other: they run the same job on the same devices with the same metadata and learned parameters, so they always produce the same result and could be one test case referenced from each phase. Variants created by `huginn reconcile` that expect a different post-change state are not reported. `validate` gains a `--parameters-dir` option to choose where learned parameters are read from.
